This project demonstrates the implementation of Homomorphic Encryption (HE) to ensure data privacy during computational processing. The solution is divided into two main components: the *Data Holder*, responsible for encrypting the dataset using the CKKS scheme from the TenSEAL library, and the *Data Analyzer*, which performs mathematical calculations (sum, mean and variance) directly on the encrypted data. Developed in Python with the aid of the pandas library, the system enables the *Data Analyzer* to process the information without exposing it in plain text. The results are then returned to the *Data Holder* for decryption and validation. The project concludes that HE enables accurate analytical results to be obtained whilst maintaining complete confidentiality, despite the computational overhead and encryption time introduced by the technique.
